{%- comment -%}
Micropub `category` -> mf2 p-category, rendered into the .tags slot every
type partial already reserves (and that _theme-chrome.scss:45 styles for the
empty case, so a post with no categories is unchanged).

`category` is a first-class Micropub property: whatever a user tags a post
with in their client arrives here as an array. Before this, all six type
partials hardcoded an empty <span class="tags"></span> and nothing ever
emitted p-category, so every tag a user applied vanished at publish.

Not ported from the source, which hardcodes a five-entry whitelist of its own
topic tags linking to a query-string filter on its archive
(post.liquid:75-81). That list is its content, not a mechanism — Indiekit
categories are arbitrary, so this builds a real page per tag instead
(content/tags.liquid) and links every category to it.
{%- endcomment -%}
<span class="tags">
{%- comment %} The leading space inside the loop is load-bearing: without it
   adjacent tag boxes abut at 0px and only their own 6px padding separates
   the words, so two tags read as one. {% endcomment -%}
{%- for tag in category %} <a class="tag p-category" href="/tags/{{ tag | slug }}/">{{ tag }}</a>{% endfor -%}
</span>
